# Uzbekistan Native Multi-Factor Authentication (Phone SMS, E-IMZO USB Flash Drive & Mobile Token)

## Overview & Architecture

We will modernize SAPAR ERP's authentication system to support Uzbekistan national identity standards and modern corporate security practices:
1. **Phone Number Authentication (+998 XX XXX-XX-XX)**:
   - Login via **Phone + Password** or **Phone + SMS OTP** (One-Time Password via Eskiz.uz / PlayMobile / SMS.uz).
   - Phone auto-masking and instant account linking.
2. **E-IMZO USB Flash Drive / E-Token / `.pfx` Certificate Login**:
   - 1-click login using physical USB e-tokens (e-Kalit) or `.pfx` certificates from a flash drive via the local E-IMZO browser agent (`127.0.0.1:64443`).
   - Server-side cryptographic challenge-response verification matching user STIR (TIN) / JShShIR (PINFL).
3. **Mobile Token / QR-Code Login (E-IMZO Mobile App)**:
   - Scan dynamic QR code with the official **E-IMZO Mobile App** on iOS/Android or tap to approve on mobile.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as User / Accountant
    participant UI as SAPAR Frontend
    participant Agent as E-IMZO Client (127.0.0.1:64443)
    participant API as SAPAR Backend
    participant SMS as Uzbekistan SMS Gateway
    participant DB as PostgreSQL (Prisma)

    alt 1. Phone + SMS OTP Login
        User->>UI: Enter +998 (90) 123-45-67
        UI->>API: POST /api/auth/phone/send-otp
        API->>DB: Store hashed OTP with 2-min expiry
        API->>SMS: Dispatch 6-digit SMS code
        SMS-->>User: SMS: "SAPAR: Sizning tasdiqlash kodingiz: 849201"
        User->>UI: Enter OTP (849201)
        UI->>API: POST /api/auth/phone/verify-otp
        API->>DB: Validate OTP & Fetch User
        API-->>UI: Issue JWT session token + User Profile
    else 2. E-IMZO Flash Drive / USB Token Login
        User->>UI: Select "E-IMZO (USB / Flash)" tab
        UI->>Agent: List installed certificates & USB keys
        Agent-->>UI: Return list of certificates (STIR, PINFL, Org Name)
        User->>UI: Pick Certificate & Enter PIN
        UI->>API: GET /api/auth/eimzo/challenge
        API-->>UI: Issue random cryptographic nonce
        UI->>Agent: Sign nonce (PKCS#7)
        Agent-->>UI: Return PKCS#7 signed base64 payload
        UI->>API: POST /api/auth/eimzo/verify-signature
        API->>DB: Verify signature, extract STIR/PINFL, link user
        API-->>UI: Issue JWT session token + User Profile
    else 3. Mobile QR Code Login
        User->>UI: Select "QR Code (Mobile Token)" tab
        UI->>API: POST /api/auth/qr/generate-session
        API-->>UI: Return qrSessionToken & Dynamic QR Code
        User->>API: Scan QR with E-IMZO Mobile App & Confirm
        UI->>API: Long-poll / WebSocket for approval
        API-->>UI: Authorized! Issue JWT session token
    end
```

